    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.49) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.59). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against Yesavage, where a strong dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the order boost (+8%) propel him into our elite tier. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a favorable matchup against Young; his +18% SP Skill adjustment highlights a mismatch that makes him our primary anchor for HR and RBI production. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) is a notable secondary start, his ability to capitalize on Kelly\u2019s higher xERA makes him a high-floor play that should pay dividends in AVG today.\n\nWe are prioritizing speed-threats given our league-wide scarcity, which is why **Nasim Nunez** (63.18) earns a UTIL start despite hitting in the nine-hole. His adjustment for a slow-delivery pitcher (+4%) makes him a strategic upside play for stolen bases. Conversely, the toughest benching decision remains **Josh Jung** (46.02). He hovered near the marginal threshold, but the efficiency gap created by the SP Skill penalty against Messick left him on the outside looking in. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (60.19) closely, as the 1.87s pop-time from the opposing catcher slightly caps his aggressive baserunning potential, though his overall projection remains solid.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the outfield. **Kyle Tucker** (51.25) and **Andy Pages** (49.46) both face Detmers, an elite arm whose presence drags their individual projections down by 19% despite their underlying talent. While **Andy Pages** receives a minor boost for the pitcher's slow delivery, both represent \"starts by necessity\" rather than absolute optimization. We will continue to sideline **Jordan Westburg** as he recovers on the IL, and we continue to evaluate **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** as primary depth pieces should the early-game outcomes for **Coby Mayo** or **Brayan Rocchio** stall.",
